17:53:23 INFO catmaster.runtime.artifact_callback | [llm.context.message] model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online callback_run_id=019cadf7-7dda-7492-80b5-e4a4904a1cbb batch=0 idx=1 class=HumanMessage type=human payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nGenerate an isolated O₂ structure in a cubic vacuum box and prepare a VASP gas-phase relaxation input set targeting the triplet.\n\nTask detail:\n1) Create POSCAR for O2 in a ~20 Å cubic cell (>=10 Å vacuum from images). Place atoms along one axis with an initial O–O distance ~1.21 Å, centered in the box; use Cartesian coordinates.\n2) Save as `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp` (or POSCAR) under the planned layout.\n3) Run `vasp_relax_prepare` on that structure with `calc_type='gas'` and write to `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/`.\n4) Ensure INCAR explicitly targets triplet: set `ISPIN=2` and add `NUPDOWN=2` via `user_incar_settings` (or post-edit INCAR if needed). Keep gas defaults (1x1x1, ISYM=0, LREAL=False, ISIF=2, EDIFF=1e-6, EDIFFG=-0.02).\nDone criteria: the input directory contains POSCAR/INCAR/KPOINTS/POTCAR and INCAR shows NUPDOWN=2.\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Path to the created O2 structure file (e.g., structures/o2_box/O2.vasp)\n- Path to prepared VASP input directory (vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax)\n- A short text snippet (or file) confirming key INCAR settings: ISPIN=2, NUPDOWN=2, ISYM=0, LREAL=.FALSE., NSW>0, IBRION=2\n\nSuggested tools:\nbash_exec, vasp_relax_prepare\n\nReference hint:\n- If you use a manual POSCAR: lattice vectors 20 0 0 / 0 20 0 / 0 0 20; atoms at (10,10,10±0.605) in Cartesian for 1.21 Å bond length.\n- If vasp_relax_prepare overwrites INCAR, prefer passing NUPDOWN via user_incar_settings rather than editing afterward.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute isolated triplet O2 in a cubic vacuum box using VASP and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from relaxed outputs.\n- Current milestone: Execution plan approved and committed to memory (task: `plan_commit`, run: `run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- Latest run artifact: Plan/protocol invariants recorded in `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md` (no result artifact yet).\n- Next action: Generate initial O2 structure in a sufficiently large cubic box, then prepare gas-phase relaxation inputs.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Final report must include energy per atom (eV/atom) and O–O bond distance (Å) from final relaxed VASP step with provenance.\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "947be453-c938-4eac-b03c-0cc978573659", "__class__": "HumanMessage", "__type__": "human"}
