 small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Run the prepared gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation in VASP and extract final observables.\n- Current milestone: Initial isolated O2 structure and gas-phase relaxation input set were generated and verified (task: `task_01`, run: `run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- Latest run artifact: `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp`; `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2` (triplet targeting explicitly enforced via `NUPDOWN=2`); check report at `reports/o2_incar_check.txt`.\n- Next action: Execute VASP relaxation and report final energy per atom (eV/atom) plus relaxed O–O bond distance (Å) with provenance.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Final report must include energy per atom (eV/atom) and O–O bond distance (Å) from final relaxed VASP step with provenance.\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_StgbNxZkF5sAusgHN70crBHK","function":{"name":"vasp_execute_batch","arguments":"{\"input_dir\": \"vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2\", \"output_dir\": \"vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax\", \"check_interval\": 30}"}}]},{"conte