17:59:12 INFO catmaster.agents.graph | [graph.stream.messages] node=run_task field=runner_messages idx=0 payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nExecute the prepared VASP gas-phase relaxation for triplet O₂.\n\nTask detail:\nRun VASP using the prepared input deck in `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2` and write outputs under a new run directory (e.g., `vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2`). Use `vasp_execute_batch` in single-folder mode (or equivalent) pointing at the input directory. After completion, verify the run terminated cleanly (look for typical VASP end-of-run markers) and that the output directory contains at least `OUTCAR`, `CONTCAR`, and `OSZICAR` (and `vasprun.xml` if produced). Do not modify INCAR unless the run fails; if it fails, capture the error snippet and stop.\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Workspace-relative path to the VASP run output directory.\n- Confirmation whether VASP finished successfully (clean termination vs error), with brief evidence (e.g., last lines of OUTCAR/OSZICAR).\n- List of key output files present: OUTCAR, CONTCAR, OSZICAR (and vasprun.xml if available).\n\nSuggested tools:\nvasp_execute_batch, bash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- Prepared inputs are in `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2`.\n- No `vasp_runs/` exists yet; create one and run there or let the executor create output dir depending on tool behavior.\n- Triplet targeting already enforced via `ISPIN=2` and `NUPDOWN=2` in INCAR; avoid changing unless SCF fails.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Run the prepared gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation in VASP and extract final observables.\n- Current milestone: Initial isolated O2 structure and gas-phase relaxation input set were generated and verified (task: `task_01`, run: `run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- Latest run artifact: `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp`; `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2` (triplet targeting explicitly enforced via `NUPDOWN=2`); check report at `reports/o2_incar_check.txt`.\n- Next action: Execute VASP relaxation and report final energy per atom (eV/atom) plus relaxed O–O bond distance (Å) with provenance.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Final report must include energy per atom (eV/atom) and O–O bond distance (Å) from final relaxed VASP step with provenance.\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "5100b4dc-0c43-4fad-847e-83b0f457cdc9"}
