ntial questions.\n- Merge-first policy for `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`:\n  - Do NOT append blindly. Canonicalize and merge before writing.\n  - Treat `PATH` as the merge key (workspace-relative, normalized form).\n  - If a `PATH` entry already exists, update that record (kind/desc/source) instead of adding a duplicate line.\n  - Keep at most 1 canonical record per `PATH`.\n  - Keep `source` concise and deduplicated (prefer latest run/task context; avoid long source history).\n  - Exclude routine internal audit logs (`metadata/**`, `audit/**`, `.logs/**`) unless they are uniquely required evidence.\n  - Include scripts only when they are primary/reusable scripts referenced by summary/facts.\n  - Exclude intermediate scratch files and one-off patch helpers unless they are required for scientific reproducibility.\n  - Prefer scientific reusable artifacts over run-noise.\n- Conflict precedence:\n  - If `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` conflicts with `FACTS.md` or `FILES.md`, topic files are authoritative.\n  - Keep single-source updates; avoid duplicating the same fact/path across multiple files.\n- Quality checks before output:\n  - Ensure detailed facts and path inventories are not dumped into `MEMORY/MEMORY.md`.\n  - Ensure key claims include evidence path pointers.\n  - Ensure `FILES.md` path records follow the `- PATH:` style where applicable.\n  - Ensure `FILES.md` has no duplicate `PATH` records after merge.\n  - Ensure `QUESTIONS.md` reflects Active vs Resolved transitions when answers are available.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"\nRun id: run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c\nTask id: task_02\nTask goal (short): Execute the prepared VASP gas-phase relaxation for triplet O₂.\nOutcome: success\n\nTask structured result (JSON):\n{\"summary\": \"Executed VASP for prepared triplet O2 gas-phase relaxation using single-folder batch mode from `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2`. Run completed successfully with clean termination markers in OUTCAR and required output files present under `vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2`.\", \"facts\": [\"VASP execution used `vasp_execute_batch` with input_dir=`vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2` and output_dir=`vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax`, producing output folder `vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2`.\", \"OUTCAR contains clean completion markers: `reached required accuracy - stopping structural energy minimisation` (line 4928) and `General timing and accounting informations for this job` (line 4944).\", \"OSZICAR tail shows final ionic step entry `4 F= -.98846517E+01 ... mag=     2.0000`, consistent with converged triplet run output.\", \"Key files present in run directory: OUTCAR, CONTCAR, OSZICAR, and vasprun.xml.\"], \"files\": [{\"path\": \"vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2\", \"description\": \"Completed VASP run directory for gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation.\", \"kind\": \"dir\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/OUTCAR\", \"description\": \"Main VASP output containing convergence and termination markers.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/OSZICAR\", \"description\": \"Electronic/ionic step log with final F and magnetic moment entries.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/CONTCAR\", \"description\": \"Final relaxed structure.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/vasprun.xml\", \"description\": \"XML run record produced by VASP.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}], \"constraints\": [], \"open_questions\": [], \"decisions\": [{\"decision\": \"Did not modify INCAR.\", \"rationale\": \"Run succeeded cleanly on first execution, so failure-handling edits were unnecessary.\"}], \"next_steps\": [\"If needed for downstream reporting, extract final energy/atom and O–O bond length from `OUTCAR`/`CONTCAR` in `vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2`.\"], \"artifacts\": [\"_tool_outputs/vasp_execute_batch/vasp_execute_batch_20260302T095844609653Z_d4c81d2e.json\", \"_tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260302T095900314327Z_54ffc128.json\"]}\n\nEditable file snapshot (authoritative):\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/MEMORY.md\">\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Run the prepared gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation in VASP and extract final observables.\n- Current milestone: Initial isolated O2 structure and gas-phase relaxation input set were generated and verified (task: `task_01`, run: `run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- Latest run artifact: `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp`; `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2` (triplet targeting explicitly enforced via `NUPDOWN=2`); check report at `reports/o2_incar_check.txt`.\n- Next action: Execute VASP relaxation and report final energy per atom (eV/atom) plus relaxed O–O bond distance (Å) with provenance.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Final report must include energy per atom (eV/atom) and O–O bond distance (Å) from final relaxed VASP step with provenance.\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Goal / principles: MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\">\n# GOAL\n\n## TL;DR\n- Primary objective: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Definition of success: Converged gas-phase O2 relaxation with reported final energy per atom and final bond length, each with output-file provenance.\n- Non-goals: (unchanged)\n\n## Objectives\n- Run a defensible VASP relaxation workflow for isolated O2 in vacuum.\n- Extract reusable final observables: total energy, energy per atom, and O–O bond length.\n\n## Success Criteria\n- VASP relaxation completes with acceptable convergence behavior (electronic + ionic).\n- Final energy per atom is reported in eV/atom from the final ionic step.\n- Final O–O bond distance is reported in Å from relaxed structure coordinates.\n- Report includes provenance (which file and final step index were used).\n\n## Non-goals\n- (empty)\n\n## Change log\n- [2026-03-02] Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- [2026-03-02] Added concrete success criteria and provenance requirement for final reported observables.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\">\n# FACTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Canonical definitions: Energy-per-atom and bond-length reporting definitions for this O2 task.\n- Verified facts: Baseline protocol is approved, and initial isolated O2 structure plus gas-phase VASP input set are prepared with explicit triplet targeting.\n- Tentative hypotheses: (empty)\n\n## Canonical Definitions\n- **Energy per atom (this task):** `E_per_atom = E_final_ionic_step / 2` for O2, units `eV/atom`.\n- **Final O–O bond length (this task):** distance between the two O atoms in the relaxed final structure (typically from `CONTCAR`), units `Å`.\n\n## Verified Facts\n- [2026-03-02 | method invariant] Approved baseline protocol for isolated O2 (triplet) in vacuum:\n  - Spin targeting: `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`.\n  - Cell model: cubic box with ~10 Å vacuum padding (about 20 Å lattice).\n  - Baseline settings from MPRelaxSet: PBE-level defaults including `ENCUT=520 eV`, `PREC=Accurate`, `LASPH=.TRUE.`.\n  - Gas-phase preset choices: `calc_type='gas'` with `Γ-only (1×1×1)`, `ISYM=0`, `LREAL=False`, `ISIF=2`.\n  - Ionic relaxation intent: `IBRION=2`, `NSW>0`, tight `EDIFF` (`1e-6`), `EDIFFG` around `-0.02 eV/Å` (acceptable range noted `-0.01` to `-0.02 eV/Å`).\n  - Dispersion correction: off (single isolated molecule in vacuum).\n  - Evidence: task structured result (`task_id=plan_commit`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- [2026-03-02 | result invariant] Isolated O2 structure generated at `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp` with a `20×20×20 Å` lattice; O Cartesian positions are `z=9.395 Å` and `z=10.605 Å`, giving a `1.21 Å` bond centered in the box.\n  - Evidence: `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp`; task structured result (`task_id=task_01`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- [2026-03-02 | result invariant] Gas-phase relaxation input set prepared at `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2` containing `POSCAR`, `INCAR`, `KPOINTS`, and `POTCAR`.\n  - Evidence: task structured result (`task_id=task_01`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- [2026-03-02 | result invariant] Prepared INCAR was verified to include `IBRION=2`, `NSW=500`, `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `ISYM=0`, and `LREAL=False`.\n  - Evidence: `reports/o2_incar_check.txt`; task structured result (`task_id=task_01`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- [2026-03-02 | acceptance invariant] Planned validation checks for production run:\n  - Force convergence target at or below `0.02 eV/Å`.\n  - No obvious SCF failure patterns during relaxation.\n  - Evidence: task structured result (`task_id=plan_commit`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n\n## Tentative\n- (empty)\n\n## Decision Log\n- [2026-03-02] **Plan committed** for execution.\n  - Rationale: Approved for execution.\n  - Evidence: task structured result (`task_id=plan_commit`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- [2026-03-02] **Post-edited INCAR to enforce `NUPDOWN=2` explicitly.**\n  - Rationale: `vasp_relax_prepare` in this environment did not expose `user_incar_settings`; explicit post-edit preserves the triplet-targeting invariant.\n  - Evidence: `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2/INCAR`; `reports/o2_incar_check.txt`; task structured result (`task_id=task_01`, `run_id=run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\">\n# FILES\n\n## TL;DR\n- Entry points: `structures/o2_box/O2.vasp`; `vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2`\n- Primary artifacts: prepared gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation inputs and INCAR verification report.\n\n## Index\n- PATH: structures/o2_box/O2.vasp | kind=output | desc=Isolated O2 structure in a 20 Å cubic vacuum box (Cartesian coordinates; 1.21 Å bond) | source=task_01\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2 | kind=dir | desc=Prepared VASP gas-phase relaxation input set containing POSCAR/INCAR/KPOINTS/POTCAR | source=task_01\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_gas_relax/O2/INCAR | kind=artifact | desc=INCAR for gas-phase relaxation with explicit triplet targeting (`ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`) | source=task_01\n- PATH: reports/o2_incar_check.txt | kind=report | desc=Verification snippet confirming key INCAR tags for the prepared O2 gas-phase run | source=task_01\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\">\n# CONSTRAINTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Hard constraints:\n  - (empty)\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- (empty)\n\n## Soft Preferences\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\">\n# QUESTIONS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Active blockers: (empty)\n\n## Active\n- (empty)\n\n## Resolved\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\">\n# RUNBOOK\n\n## TL;DR\n- Standard operating procedure pointer file.\n\n## Checklist\n1. Confirm goal and success criteria from task packet.\n2. Read MEMORY.md first, then locate details via rg/sed.\n3. Persist large outputs to files and cite paths.\n4. Finish by returning one structured TaskOutput response.\n\n</editable_file>\n","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"high","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"prompt_cache_re