18:01:12 INFO catmaster.runtime.artifact_callback | [llm.parsed_tool_call] model=openai/gpt-5.2:online callback_run_id=019cadfe-7697-7081-9ea9-f46cb6d298c9 gen=0 cand=0 call=0 name=DirectorOutput args_json={"state": "PerformNextTask", "rationale": "VASP run is complete; only remaining requirement is to parse final TOTEN and relaxed O–O bond length with clear provenance and produce a summary artifact. Previous extraction had a minor script error that omitted the provenance line, so rerun extraction cleanly.", "perform_next_task": {"task_packet": {"goal": "Parse VASP outputs for final total energy, energy per atom, and relaxed O–O bond distance with provenance.", "task_detail": "Use vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/{OUTCAR,OSZICAR,CONTCAR,vasprun.xml}. Extract the last ionic-step TOTEN (eV) from OUTCAR, record the exact matching line and its line number, and compute energy per atom = TOTEN/2. Compute O–O bond distance from CONTCAR using minimum-image convention (cell is 20 Å). Cross-check TOTEN against the last OSZICAR F= value (optional but helpful). Write a concise machine-readable summary file (e.g., analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.json) and a human-readable txt (analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.txt) including provenance (file names + line numbers). Done when the summary files exist and values are printed in stdout.", "expected_outputs": ["Printed stdout lines: final TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), O–O bond length (Å), and OUTCAR provenance line with line number.", "analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.json created with keys: toten_eV, energy_per_atom_eV, oo_bond_A, provenance (outcar_line_no, outcar_line_text, contcar_path).", "analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.txt created with the same values in readable form.", "(Optional) OSZICAR last line value to validate consistency."], "suggested_tools": ["bash_exec"], "reference_hint": ["OUTCAR pattern: \"free  energy   TOTEN\" (take the last occurrence).", "OSZICAR last ionic step contains \"F=\" value; should match TOTEN within rounding