all windows (no large file dumps).\n- Internal metadata audit logs are not task inputs; do not read or reference them in task reasoning.\n- By default, do not generate long markdown reports via `cat <<'MD'`.\n\nParsing policy:\n- Debug triage should prioritize focused, minimal evidence extraction and concise failure signatures.\n- For extracting final numerical results across many calculations (for comparison/reporting), avoid repeated manual grep stitching; prefer parser libraries or small single-purpose scripts.\n- Prefer mature third-party libraries for parsing and post-analysis when available; avoid reimplementing standard parsers/analysis logic from scratch.\n- Common Python packages are available and preferred when relevant: ase, pymatgen, numpy, matplotlib, scipy, pandas, fitz, requests.\n- For actual workload execution (batch processing, long runs, or outputs to be reused/audited), write reusable script files and keep each script focused/small.\n\nTermination and handoff:\n- End with one concise final handoff that clearly states the task status and reusable outputs.\n- Use `status=\"done\"` when task is complete.\n- Use `status=\"blocked\"` only when still blocked after bounded self-adjustment attempts on non-critical execution parameters, or when hard scientific invariants conflict.\n- Follow schema field descriptions for per-field content quality and placeholders; do not fill fields with invented content.\n- For remote/batch job failures, do one minimal triage (failing status file, stdout/stderr snippets, key inputs) and attempt one focused fix.\n- Do not do open-ended exploration for remote failures (no SSH). If failure persists, return `status=\"blocked\"` with failed paths, evidence pointers, likely cause, and a minimal rerun/repair plan that reruns only the failed subset.\n- Keep handoff evidence-based and concise; avoid redundant repetition across fields.\n- Function tools must be invoked via tool calls. Do NOT put function tool names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nParse VASP outputs for final total energy, energy per atom, and relaxed O–O bond distance with provenance.\n\nTask detail:\nUse vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/{OUTCAR,OSZICAR,CONTCAR,vasprun.xml}. Extract the last ionic-step TOTEN (eV) from OUTCAR, record the exact matching line and its line number, and compute energy per atom = TOTEN/2. Compute O–O bond distance from CONTCAR using minimum-image convention (cell is 20 Å). Cross-check TOTEN against the last OSZICAR F= value (optional but helpful). Write a concise machine-readable summary file (e.g., analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.json) and a human-readable txt (analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.txt) including provenance (file names + line numbers). Done when the summary files exist and values are printed in stdout.\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Printed stdout lines: final TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), O–O bond length (Å), and OUTCAR provenance line with line number.\n- analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.json created with keys: toten_eV, energy_per_atom_eV, oo_bond_A, provenance (outcar_line_no, outcar_line_text, contcar_path).\n- analysis/o2_gas_relax/summary.txt created with the same values in readable form.\n- (Optional) OSZICAR last line value to validate consistency.\n\nSuggested tools:\nbash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- OUTCAR pattern: \"free  energy   TOTEN\" (take the last occurrence).\n- OSZICAR last ionic step contains \"F=\" value; should match TOTEN within rounding.\n- CONTCAR is a POSCAR-format file; compute minimum-image distance for two atoms.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Extract final observables from the completed gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation.\n- Current milestone: VASP gas-phase triplet O2 relaxation completed successfully with clean termination markers (task: `task_02`, run: `run_20260302_095018_3a4d0c`).\n- Latest run artifact: `vasp_runs/o2_gas_relax/O2/{OUTCAR,OSZICAR,CONTCAR,vasprun.xml}`.\n- Next action: Parse final ionic-step total energy to report energy per atom (eV/atom) and measure relaxed O–O bond distance (Å) from final structure with provenance.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Final report must include energy per atom (eV/atom) and O–O bond distance (Å) from final relaxed VASP step with provenance.\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"medium","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"required","tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","description":"Build a 3D molecule from a SMILES string using RDKit. Specially, pay attention to the formal charge of the SMILES string, RDkit will check the charge and add Hs to the molecule to make it neutral.","parameters":{"properties":{"smiles":{"description":"SMILES string for the molecule.","type":"string"},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional base name for output files; defaults to formula."},"output_path":{"default":"mol","description":"Workspace-relative path prefix; files will be <prefix>.xyz and/or <prefix>.vasp.","type":"string"},"box_padding":{"default":10.0,"description":"Padding (Å) added around the molecule to make a cubic box for POSCAR. Box lattice is around twice the padding value (10A Padding -> 20A Box).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar (with PBC box), xyz (no PBC), or both.","pattern":"^(poscar|xyz|both)$","type":"string"}},"required":["smiles"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_relax_batch","description":"Submit multiple MACE relaxations in one DPDispatcher submission. Preferred tool for batch MACE relaxations.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Root directory containing structure files with lattice (POSCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory to store batch outputs. Results mirror the input directory structure; each input file expands to a folder without suffix (e.g. input_dir/a/c.vasp -> output_root/a/c/opt.vasp). Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"fmax":{"default":0.02,"description":"Force threshold for relaxation in eV/Angstrom.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"maxsteps":{"default":500,"description":"Max steps for relaxation.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name. Recommended options: 'mh-1' (slower, higher accuracy) or 'medium-mpa-0' (faster, lower accuracy).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models (e.g. 'omat_pbe'). Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction in mace_mp. Default: false.","type":"boolean"},"relax_lattice":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax lattice/cell together with atomic positions via ASE FrechetCellFilter.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_sp_batch","description":"Run MACE single-point jobs for structures under one directory.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory containing structures (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF/VASP).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Output root for batch results. Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name (e.g., mh-1, medium-mpa-0).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models. Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP relax inputs with calc_type presets and k_product k-mesh.\n    Also can be modified for other calculation types by overriding INCAR via the user_incar_settings.\n    Support exts: .vasp, .cif\n\n    Baseline DFT settings follow Materials Project MPRelaxSet (key defaults):\n    - PBE54 POTCARS, ENCUT=520 eV, PREC=Accurate, ISPIN=2, IBRION=2, LREAL=AUTO, LASPH=True, LWAVE=False, LCHARG=False.\n    - Additional overrides applied based on calc_type: ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.1 for bulk/slab; ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.01 for gas.\n    - ISIF policy: bulk with relax_cell=False -> ISIF=2; bulk with relax_cell=True -> ISIF=3.\n      slab and gas always use ISIF=2, where slab forces KPOINTS z=1 and gas forces KPOINTS 1x1x1 with ISYM=0, LREAL=False.\n    - Improved convergence settings: EDIFF=1e-6; NSW=500; EDIFFG=-0.02;\n    - LORBIT is controlled by compute_dos (default False -> LORBIT=0, True -> LORBIT=11).\n    - KPOINTS is generated by k*a=k_product, where a is the lattice constant in Angstrom. Set to 30 by default and sufficient for most systems.\n    - DFT-D3 and DFT+U are disabled by default. Enable them if the system is adsorption system(DFT-D3) or transition metal oxide system(DFT+U).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Path to a structure file with lattice information (POSCAR/CIF) or a directory containing multiple structures. Support exts: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per input structure). If input_path is a file: output_root/<stem>/...; if input_path is a directory, preserve relative subfolders: output_root/<relpath>/<stem>/...","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation type: 'gas'|'bulk'|'slab'. This provides preset INCAR overrides for different calculation types. gas is suitable for small molecules; slab is suitable for surface slab models; bulk is suitable for bulk relaxations.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"relax_cell":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax cell shape/volume (ISIF=3). Only valid when calc_type='bulk'.","type":"boolean"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"Target k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1, forced odd (Gamma-centered); gas always 1x1x1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 Correction (IVDW=11). Enable it for adsorption calculations.","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U relevant settings according to materials project standard. Enable it for Transition Metal Oxide systems.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0) to reduce disk usage.","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass of cell in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LREAL\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_sp_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP single-point inputs for structures under a file or directory. Parameters are the same as VaspRelaxPrepareInput, but with single_point relaxation enabled (NSW=0, IBRION=-1).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Structure file or directory of structures. Supported: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per structure).","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation preset for k-mesh and INCAR defaults.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 correction (IVDW=11).","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U settings.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0).","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LORBIT\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"build_slab","description":"Build slabs for all terminations of a Miller index from bulk structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of bulk_structure or bulk_dir. When bulk_dir is used, output_root is required.\n    Batch outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path\n    (without suffix) using '__'.","parameters":{"properties":{"bulk_structure":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"bulk_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing bulk structure files for batch slab building."},"miller_index":{"description":"Miller index [h,k,l].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_root":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory to write the slab structures. Required for bulk_dir; defaults to 'slabs' for single file. For bulk_dir, outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"slab_thickness":{"default":12.0,"description":"Target slab thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"vacuum_thickness":{"default":15.0,"description":"Vacuum thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"supercell":{"default":[1,1,1],"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c] for slab structure after generation.","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"get_symmetry_slab":{"default":false,"description":"If true, returned slabs will ensure top and bottom surfaces are identical. Use it for surface energy calculation.","type":"boolean"},"orthogonal":{"default":false,"description":"If true, convert each slab to an orthogonal c-oriented cell. Useful for grain boundary generation.","type":"boolean"},"lll_reduce":{"default":false,"description":"Apply LLL reduction during slab generation. Not recommended to use unless necessary.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["miller_index"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_layers","description":"Fix (freeze) the bottom N atomic layers of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_layers.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"freeze_layers":{"description":"Number of bottom layers to freeze. Use layer_tol to group layers.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c before applying constraints.","type":"boolean"},"layer_tol":{"default":0.2,"description":"Layer grouping tolerance in Å. 0.2 is suitable for most cases except for highly tilted slabs.","exclusiveMinimum":0.0,"type":"number"}},"required":["freeze_layers"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_height","description":"Fix (freeze) atoms within specified z ranges of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_height.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"z_ranges":{"description":"Ranges in Å in Cartesian coordinates; atoms in these z ranges are frozen.","items":{"properties":{"z_min":{"description":"Lower bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"},"z_max":{"description":"Upper bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"}},"required":["z_min","z_max"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c after applying constraints.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["z_ranges"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"supercell","description":"Create supercells from structure file(s). THIS WILL LOSE ALL SELECTIVE DYNAMICS INFORMATION.\n    Provide exactly one of structure_file or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<structure_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_supercell.json.\n\n    The JSON format is:\n    {\n      \"results\": [\n        {\"input_rel\": \"a/CO.vasp\", \"structure_id\": \"a__CO\", \"output_rel\": \"out/a__CO.vasp\", \"natoms\": 2}\n      ]\n    }","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing structure files for batch supercell generation."},"supercell":{"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path for single structure (workspace-relative, e.g., bulk_supercell.vasp)."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<structure_id>.vasp where structure_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."}},"required":["supercell"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"enumerate_adsorption_sites","description":"Enumerate adsorption sites on a slab using ASF. Use it only for small scale placement.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_json:\n    [\n      {\"label\": \"ontop_0\", \"kind\": \"ontop\", \"cart_coords\": [x, y, z]}\n    ]\n    The returned tool data includes the workspace-relative path in \"sites\" and \"sites_json_rel\".","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF), workspace-relative.","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"Which site families to return: all|ontop|bridge|hollow.","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height above surface to sample adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_json":{"default":"adsorption/sites.json","description":"Output JSON path for site list (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"place_adsorbate","description":"Place an adsorbate molecule on a slab. Use it only if for small scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    It writes metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json and an ads_indices index JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"site":{"default":"auto","description":"Site label like ontop_0|bridge_1|hollow_2 or 'auto' (which