nal energy per atom and final bond length, each with output-file provenance.\n- Non-goals: (unchanged)\n\n## Objectives\n- Run a defensible VASP relaxation workflow for isolated O2 in vacuum.\n- Extract reusable final observables: total energy, energy per atom, and O–O bond length.\n\n## Success Criteria\n- VASP relaxation completes with acceptable convergence behavior (electronic + ionic).\n- Final energy per atom is reported in eV/atom from the final ionic step.\n- Final O–O bond distance is reported in Å from relaxed structure coordinates.\n- Report includes provenance (which file and final step index were used).\n\n## Non-goals\n- (empty)\n\n## Change log\n- [2026-03-02] Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- [2026-03-02] Added concrete success criteria and provenance requirement for final reported observables.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\">\n# FACTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Canonical definitions: Energy-per-atom and bond-length reporting definitions for this O2 task.\n- Verified facts: Baseline triplet O2 gas-phase protocol was prepared and then executed successfully in VASP with clean completion markers and expected output files.\n- Tentative hypotheses: (empty)\n\n## Canonical Definitions\n- **Energy per atom (this task):** `E_per_atom = E_final_ionic_step / 2` for O2, units `eV/atom`.\n- **Final O–O bond length (this task):** distance between the two O atoms in the relaxed final structure (typically from `CONTCAR`), units `Å`.\n\n## Verified Facts\n- [2026-03-02 | method invariant] Approved baseline protocol for isolated O2 (triplet) in vacuum:\n  - Spin targeting: `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`.\n  - Cell model: cubic box with ~10 Å vacuum padding (about 20 Å lattice).\n  - Baseline settings from MPRelaxSet: PBE-level defaults including `ENCUT=520 eV`, `PREC=Accurate`, `LASPH=.TRUE.`.\n  - Gas-phase